WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.225
Not acting doesn't mean standing still.

2
00:00:02.225 --> 00:00:03.950
Three things happen by default.

3
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:07.113
First, money gets spent
without a choice being made.

4
00:00:07.113 --> 00:00:12.224
The BOD 26-02 refresh will
happen on a directive clock.

5
00:00:12.224 --> 00:00:15.889
Run as like-for-like replacement,
it spends the money and closes

6
00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:19.413
the architecture question for
the life of the new equipment.

7
00:00:19.413 --> 00:00:21.426
Deferral has a measured price too.

8
00:00:21.426 --> 00:00:28.354
GAO reported that billing for six agencies'
legacy Networx contracts rose from about

9
00:00:28.354 --> 00:00:32.062
13.4 million dollars in
February 2025 to about

10
00:00:32.062 --> 00:00:35.575
40.9 million in March,
a 206 percent increase.

11
00:00:35.575 --> 00:00:39.763
Second, gaps surface as findings
rather than accepted risks.

12
00:00:39.763 --> 00:00:44.238
The technical situation is identical;
the institutional position isn't.

13
00:00:44.238 --> 00:00:48.663
And cutting managed TIC circuits
before CISA confirms replacement

14
00:00:48.663 --> 00:00:53.012
telemetry trades a transport gap for
a visibility gap, which is worse.

15
00:00:53.012 --> 00:00:55.551
Third, cost gets blamed on the cloud.

16
00:00:55.551 --> 00:00:58.758
When workloads migrate before
transport is measured,

17
00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:03.250
slowness gets blamed on the only thing
being measured, and cloud spend rises.

18
00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:08.275
The book labels that its own inference,
a hypothesis to test in your estate.

19
00:01:08.275 --> 00:01:11.825
And under all three, the
governor is attack surface.

20
00:01:11.825 --> 00:01:16.744
In February 2026, Emergency
Directive 26-03 ordered action

21
00:01:16.744 --> 00:01:21.563
on Cisco SD-WAN systems after
attackers compromised them.

22
00:01:21.563 --> 00:01:24.799
Whatever you buy, protect it
before it carries traffic.

23
00:01:24.799 --> 00:01:28.030
Next, what TIC 3.0 actually requires.
